flowchart TD
  U[Developer / CI] --> CLI[bin/agentf]
  CLI --> ICLI[agentf install / update]
  ICLI --> INS[Agentf::Installer]

  subgraph Source[Class Metadata Source]
    A[Agent classes\nAgentf::Agents::*]
    C[Command classes\nAgentf::Commands::*]
    T[Tool primitives\nAgentf::Tools::*]
  end

  INS --> A
  INS --> C

  A --> AMD[Generated Agent Markdown\n.opencode/agents/* OR .github/agents/*]
  C --> CMD[Generated Command Markdown\n.opencode/commands/* OR .github/commands/*]

  AMD -.includes memory policy.-> MEMMETA[memory_concepts\nreads/writes/policy]
  CMD -.lists callable commands.-> CMETA[manifest commands list]

  subgraph Runtime[Execution Runtime]
    APP[App / User Task]
    WF[Agentf::WorkflowEngine\nORCHESTRATOR]
    P[Provider Adapter\nOpenCode / Copilot]
    AG[Role Agents\nPLANNER/ENGINEER/QA_TESTER/etc]
    COM[Commands]
    TOOLS[Tools / Provider Tools]
    MET[Metrics & Telemetry]
  end

  APP --> WF
  WF --> P
  P --> AG
  P --> COM
  COM --> TOOLS
  WF --> MET

  WF -->|get_relevant_context| REDIS[(RedisMemory\nRedisJSON + RediSearch)]
  WF -->|store_feature_intent| REDIS
  AG -->|store_success/pitfall/lesson| REDIS
  REDIS --> EDGE[(Edge Graph\nedge:*)]

  subgraph MemoryCLI[Memory CLI]
    MCLI[agentf memory ...]
    MR[Commands::MemoryReviewer]
  end

  MCLI --> MR
  MR -->|query/search/summaries| REDIS
  MR -->|neighbors/subgraph| EDGE
  MCLI -->|add-business-intent / add-feature-intent| REDIS

  subgraph MCP[MCP Server]
    MS[agentf mcp-server]
    MTOOLS[code and memory tools\nneighbors and subgraph]
    WEB[MCP Web UI (optional)]
  end

  MS --> MTOOLS
  MTOOLS --> COM
  MS --> WEB

  REDIS -.optional doc sync by agent behavior.-> AMD

  %% Notes: this diagram shows how metadata produces manifests, how the runtime
  %% fetches and stores context in Redis, and how MCP and CLI expose tools.
